{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BMZyRLw1FnkUJf72mWHx69","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\section{Introduction}\n2\t\n3\tLarge Language Model (LLM) judges have become central infrastructure for NLP evaluation and preference-based alignment training.\n4\tSystems such as AlpacaEval, MT-Bench, and Chatbot Arena rely on LLM judges to score and rank model outputs, and the resulting leaderboards guide both academic research and industry deployment.\n5\tReinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) and Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) pipelines consume judge-generated preferences as reward signals that shape model behavior during alignment.\n6\tThe reliability of these judgments carries direct consequences: it determines which models the community considers superior and which response patterns are reinforced.\n7\tAs automated judges increasingly mediate both evaluation and training, any systematic bias in their assessments propagates through the entire model development pipeline.\n8\t\n9\tRecent work has converged on a striking finding: \\emph{style bias} is the dominant source of unreliability in LLM judges, far outweighing other documented biases such as position or verbosity preference.\n10\t\\citet{murugadoss2025sos} show that style features alone explain judge scores with $R = 0.999$, far exceeding the explanatory power of content features.\n11\t\\citet{li2026preference} demonstrate that 76--92\\% of observed preference signals originate from surface-level style cues rather than substantive quality differences.\n12\t\\citet{soumik2026judging} report bias scores of 0.76--0.92 across five different judges.\n13\tDespite this consensus on severity, existing approaches share four critical gaps: (1)~they treat style as a single dimension, typically reducing it to response length; (2)~they rely on correlational analyses that cannot establish causal direction; (3)~population-level corrections such as length-controlled AlpacaEval \\citep{dubois2025lc} cannot diagnose per-instance bias; and (4)~no existing method provides black-box, post-hoc, per-axis interventional detection.\n14\tRecent multi-feature frameworks such as CASSE \\citep{casse2026concise} and FairJudge \\citep{wang2026fairjudge} begin to decompose style into finer dimensions, but neither provides interventional identification of per-axis effects.\n15\tA further methodological concern compounds these limitations: standard Likert pointwise scoring (integer scales from 1 to 10) suffers from a two-layer structural limitation.\n16\tFirst, integer discretization produces ${\\sim}60\\%$ uninformative ties ($\\Delta = 0$), wasting the majority of the evaluation budget.\n17\tSecond, even among the non-tied pairs, absolute Likert scoring captures weaker signal than forced pairwise comparison on identical data---a limitation that persists under ordinal regression, ruling out interval-scale assumptions as the cause.\n18\t\n19\tWe propose Causal Style Decomposition (CSD), a framework that addresses all four gaps.\n20\tDrawing on causal inference methods for text \\citep{veitch2020adapting}, CSD operates in three stages: binary style-controlled rewriting along a single axis (e.g., formal vs.\\ casual), content preservation verification through Natural Language Inference (NLI) entailment scoring, and bias measurement via position-controlled pairwise comparison.\n21\tBecause CSD requires no access to judge internals and applies post-hoc to any black-box judge, it complements existing population-level approaches and provides finer-grained, per-instance diagnostics.\n22\tOur approach provides interventional rather than formal causal evidence; we present an assumed data-generating process (Section~\\ref{sec:causal_framework}) but do not claim a complete structural causal model or invoke SUTVA assumptions.\n23\tOur experiments reveal what we term the \\emph{Likert Blindspot} across two architecturally distinct judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B) and two primary style axes (formality, verbosity), with directionally consistent exploratory evidence on a third axis (register).\n24\tOn the same formality data, Likert scoring yields non-significant ATE ($p = 0.332$, $p = 0.908$) for both judges, while Bradley-Terry analysis detects 63.0\\% (GPT-4o, $p < 0.001$) and 66.5\\% (Qwen3-32B, $p < 0.0001$) formal win probabilities.\n25\tThe effect is most dramatic for verbosity, where a 77.3\\% BT win probability ($p < 0.0001$) remains invisible to Likert scoring ($p = 0.179$).\n26\tFigure~\\ref{fig:forest_plot} illustrates this divergence.\n27\tUnlike LC-AlpacaEval \\citep{dubois2025lc}, which applies a single population-level length regression, CSD decomposes bias along multiple axes with per-instance style-controlled intervention.\n28\t\n29\tOur contributions are as follows:\n30\t\\begin{itemize}\n31\t    \\item \\textbf{A black-box interventional framework} for detecting per-axis style bias in LLM judges through binary style-controlled rewriting and position-controlled pairwise comparison (Section~\\ref{sec:method}).\n32\t    \\item \\textbf{The Likert Blindspot phenomenon:} demonstrated across four judge$\\times$axis configurations at $p < 0.001$---formality bias is undetectable by Likert ($p \\geq 0.33$) but significant under Bradley-Terry for both GPT-4o (63.0\\%, $p < 0.001$) and Qwen3-32B (66.5\\%, $p < 0.0001$); verbosity bias (77.3\\%, $p < 0.0001$) is similarly invisible to Likert ($p = 0.179$)---with two additional register configurations showing weaker but consistent patterns (Section~\\ref{sec:experiments}, Table~\\ref{tab:main_results}).\n33\t    \\item \\textbf{The sensitivity hierarchy:} seven statistical methods applied to the same data confirm the Blindspot is inherent to Likert measurement---all Likert-based methods fail regardless of statistical approach, while both pairwise methods detect the effect (Section~\\ref{sec:analysis}, Table~\\ref{tab:sensitivity}).\n34\t    \\item \\textbf{Practical implications for evaluation methodology:} style bias audits should employ pairwise comparison rather than Likert scoring, and bias must be assessed per axis rather than as a single ``style'' factor (Section~\\ref{sec:conclusion}).\n35\t\\end{itemize}\n36\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HCHAwzsHRvvesX9nb28xmb","session_id":"6668cb44-b8d1-40b2-9a3f-1ea035cc3371","uuid":"153e1b77-ea5d-4e59-8ae1-1127e6e7f6fd","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:06:22.748Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PvqXmdEYxMTvbGBWvRqnrB","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/memory.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Memory — causal_style_decomp_judge\\\\n\\\\n## 服务器环境 (westb-29275)\\\\n- SSH: `causal_style_decomp_judge`（~/.ssh/config 别名，免密）\\\\n- GPU: 4× RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell 96GB, torch=2.11.0+cu130\\\\n- 环境: aml-train 镜像, conda base (`source /root/miniconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh && conda activate base`)\\\\n- 数据盘: `/root/autodl-tmp/` 250GB\\\\n- **网络**: AutoDL 网络受限，每次 SSH 会话需 `source /etc/network_turbo`\\\\n- **CUDA JIT**: `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` 需包含 `/root/miniconda3/lib/python3.12/site-packages/nvidia/cu13/lib`\\\\n- **GPU 3 有驱动异常**（100% util/0 MiB），不可用，只用 GPU 0-2\\\\n- **HF 网络**: 必须设 `TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1` 避免 HF Hub 请求挂起\\\\n\\\\n## 模型路径\\\\n- NLI: `/root/autodl-tmp/models/nli-deberta-v3-large/`\\\\n- BERTScore: `microsoft/deberta-xlarge-mnli` 在 HF cache `/root/autodl-tmp/.hf_cache/`\\\\n- Qwen3-8B: `/root/autodl-tmp/models/Qwen3-8B/`\\\\n- Qwen3-32B: `/root/autodl-tmp/models/Qwen3-32B/` ✅ 完成（17 shards, 62GB）\\\\n\\\\n## API 配置\\\\n- **统一 proxy endpoint**: `http://47.94.22.126/v1`\\\\n- GPT-4o: key_id=`openai_api_key_direct` — ✅ 可用\\\\n- Claude Sonnet 4: key_id=`claude_api_key` — ❌ 代理不支持\\\\n- Gemini 2.0 Flash: key_id=`gemini_api_key` — ❌ 代理不支持\\\\n- **只有 OpenAI 可通过代理使用**，Claude/Gemini 需直接 API key\\\\n\\\\n## 数据\\\\n- MVP 数据: `/root/causal_style_decomp_judge/data/mvp_samples.jsonl` (100 条, seed=42)\\\\n- Pipeline 输出目录: `/root/causal_style_decomp_judge/data/`\\\\n- exp-005 RATE control: `data/rate_control_input.jsonl` (88 条, NLI≥0.90 过滤)\\\\n- Verified datasets: `verified_32b.jsonl`(100), `verified_verbosity.jsonl`(86 NLI-pass), `verified_register.jsonl`(94 NLI-pass), `verified_alpacaeval.jsonl`(86 NLI-pass), `verified_mtbench.jsonl`(73 NLI-pass)\\\\n\\\\n## RATE 方法 axis 可行性梯度（核心发现）\\\\n\\\\n| Axis | 改变了什么 | NLI 策略 | Pass rate | 结论 |\\\\n|------|-----------|----------|-----------|------|\\\\n| Formality | 表面 register | Bidirectional min(fwd,bwd) | 88% ✅ | 完全可行 |\\\\n| Verbosity | 信息量 | Direction-aware (D012/D013) | 86% ✅ | 需 NLI-only gate + direction-aware |\\\\n| Register | 话语情境 | NLI-only (D019) | 95% ✅ | NLI-only gate，与 formality 正交 (50%) |\\\\n| Tone | 认知承诺 | Bidirectional | 45% ❌ | 结构性不可行 |\\\\n\\\\n**D023 决策：所有 axis 统一使用 NLI-only gating**（threshold 0.90）。\\\\n\\\\n## NLI Gate 特性（exp-013 发现）\\\\n\\\\nNLI gate (DeBERTa-v3-large, threshold 0.90) 是 **precision-oriented conservative filter**：\\\\n- Precision 98.9%, Recall 91.6%, PABAK=0.82, AC1=0.89\\\\n- Kappa paradox（Feinstein & Cicchetti 1990）：base rate 88:12 → kappa=0.43 低估\\\\n\\\\n## 完整 2×3 矩阵（C1/C2/C3/C4 核心 evidence）\\\\n\\\\n### Blindspot 矩阵\\\\n\\\\n| Judge | Axis | BT P(style) | BT p | Likert p | Tie Rate | Blindspot? |\\\\n|-------|------|-------------|------|----------|----------|------------|\\\\n| GPT-4o | Formality | 63.0% | <0.001 | 0.332 | 62.5% | ✅ |\\\\n| GPT-4o | **Verbosity** | **76.0%** | **0.0001** | **0.403** | 58.1% | **✅** |\\\\n| GPT-4o | Register | 57.0% | 0.04 | 0.785 | 64.9% | ✅ |\\\\n| Qwen3-32B | Formality | 66.5% | <0.0001 | 0.908 | 72.7% | ✅ |\\\\n| Qwen3-32B | **Verbosity** | **77.3%** | **<0.0001** | **0.179** | 58.1% | **✅** |\\\\n| Qwen3-32B | Register | 59.3% | 0.220 | 0.505 | 63.8% | — |\\\\n\\\\n**5/6 cells Blindspot confirmed**。唯一例外：Qwen3-32B register pairwise p=0.22 不显著。\\\\n\\\\n### GEE Decomposition 完整 Gradient\\\\n\\\\n| Judge | Axis | Style OR | Style p | Orig OR | Orig p | 解读 |\\\\n|-------|------|----------|---------|---------|--------|------|\\\\n| Qwen3-32B | **Verbosity** | **13.10** | 2.6e-09 | 0.49 | 0.096 ns | **纯 style bias** |\\\\n| GPT-4o | **Verbosity** | **10.97** | <0.0001 | 0.44 | 0.051 ns | **纯 style bias** |\\\\n| Qwen3-32B | Formality | 4.20 | 0.0002 | 4.70 | <0.0001 | Style ≈ Orig |\\\\n| GPT-4o | Formality | 2.21 | 0.010 | 1.82 | 0.052 | Style > Orig |\\\\n| GPT-4o | Register | 1.88 | 0.028 | 2.21 | 0.006 | Orig > Style |\\\\n| Qwen3-32B | Register | 1.91 | 0.046 | 5.72 | <0.0001 | Orig >> Style |\\\\n\\\\n### 跨模型一致性（论文核心 argument）\\\\n- **Verbosity**: 两模型 Style OR=10-13，Orig OR<1 ns → **纯 style bias 是 model-independent**\\\\n- **Register**: 两模型 Style OR≈1.9 → **几乎相同的边缘 style effect**\\\\n- **Formality**: Qwen3-32B 双效应更强但 pattern 一致\\\\n\\\\n### C3 Axis Gradient\\\\n- **Verbosity = 纯 style bias**（OR=10-13，originality ns 且反向）\\\\n- **Formality = 混合效应**（style + originality 共存）\\\\n- **Register = originality 主导**（style 边缘）\\\\n\\\\n## Verbosity vs Formality 的方向不对称性差异（关键机制洞察）\\\\n\\\\n**Verbosity = 真正的 style bias**（非 originality bias）：\\\\n- verbose→concise: 80.6% prefer original（verbose）\\\\n- concise→verbose: 90.7% prefer rewrite（verbose）\\\\n- 两个方向都偏好 verbose content → 真正的 verbosity preference\\\\n\\\\n**Formality = 可能混合 originality bias**：\\\\n- formal→casual: 81.4% prefer original (p<0.0001)\\\\n- casual→formal: 50.0% (p=1.0, 无偏好)\\\\n- GPT-4o 模式类似但不极端：78.8% vs 54.5%\\\\n\\\\n**Register = 主要是 originality bias**：\\\\n- academic→conv: 89.3% prefer original\\\\n- conv→academic: 68.8% prefer original\\\\n\\\\n## BT Canonical 数字 (D032)\\\\n\\\\n- **NLI-filtered (primary)**: P(formal)=63.0%, CI [55.8%, 70.3%], p<0.001, 88 pairs/173 comp\\\\n- **All-data (robustness)**: P(formal)=60.9%, CI [53.8%, 67.8%], p=0.001, 100 pairs/197 comp\\\\n- Bootstrap: pair-level resampling\\\\n\\\\n## Power Curve Canonical (D030/D031)\\\\n\\\\n| Method | Effect Size | 80% Power n |\\\\n|--------|------------|-------------|\\\\n| Pairwise BT | p=0.630 | 114 |\\\\n| Pairwise Sign Test | p=0.739, r=0.523 | 62 |\\\\n| Binarized Likert | p=0.606, tie=0.625 | 462 |\\\\n| Likert ATE | d=0.073 (raw) | 1,473 |\\\\n\\\\n## 分析脚本路径\\\\n- BT + GEE (Qwen3-32B formality/register): `csd_pipeline/qwen32b_analysis.py`\\\\n- Verbosity GEE (Qwen3-32B): `csd_pipeline/verbosity_gee.py`\\\\n- GPT-4o 全量分析: `csd_pipeline/gpt4o_analysis.py`\\\\n- Power curve: `csd_pipeline/gen_power_curve.py`\\\\n- BT 主分析 (GPT-4o formality): `csd_pipeline/exp016_bradley_terry.py`\\\\n- Pipeline diagram: `csd_pipeline/gen_pipeline_figure.py`\\\\n- Forest plot: `csd_pipeline/gen_forest_plot.py`\\\\n\\\\n## 踩坑经验\\\\n- [2026-05-20] vLLM Qwen3 需要 `VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0`（Blackwell sm120 不兼容）\\\\n- [2026-05-20] 32B FP16 单卡 96GB OK（gpu-memory-utilization=0.90 用了 88GB）\\\\n- [2026-05-20] Pairwise position-controlled dual-trial 比 Likert 灵敏得多\\\\n- [2026-05-20] Tone axis 结构性不可行\\\\n- [2026-05-21] NLI-only gating 对所有 axis 都适用（D023）\\\\n- [2026-05-21] Power curve 用 raw d=0.073（不依赖 RATE 假设）\\\\n- [2026-05-21] Qwen3-32B tp=2 可作为 local judge，~13 分钟 3 axis\\\\n- [2026-05-21] GEE decomposition 用 exchangeable correlation（statsmodels GEE）\\\\n- [2026-05-21] vLLM kill 必须用 specific PID，不能 killall（M006 教训）\\\\n- [2026-05-21] 代理 endpoint 只支持 OpenAI，不支持 Claude/Gemini\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 6100, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bsn2XSA4ECLQpjs2VuU8SC","session_id":"6668cb44-b8d1-40b2-9a3f-1ea035cc3371","uuid":"b9da7d92-1402-400d-a7f7-e3d4e8dc7c06","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:06:22.796Z"}
